<meta type=article>
  <title | Mathematics Sweep>
</meta>

<section | Inline and display math>
Inline math such as
<!-- cell: inline-math/register:sigil -->
<$ e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0 $> flows within the line and is never numbered. A numbered
display equation:

<!-- cell: display-math/register:sigil -->
<$$ #eq:gauss | \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} e^{-x^2}\,dx = \sqrt{\pi} $$>

is cross-referenced as <ref @eq:gauss>.

<section | Environments>
The long-form environments each render their own wrapper around the KaTeX block.

<!-- cell: math/form:long -->
<math>
\sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i = X
</math>

<!-- cell: align/form:long -->
<align>
x^2 + y^2 &= z^2 \\
a + b &= c
</align>

<!-- cell: cases/form:long -->
<cases>
x^2 & \text{if } x \ge 0 \\
-x^2 & \text{otherwise}
</cases>

<!-- cell: matrix/form:long -->
<matrix>
1 & 2 \\
3 & 4
</matrix>

<!-- cell: eqnarray/form:long -->
<eqnarray>
a &=& b \\
c &=& d
</eqnarray>
